/-! ## (5.7): a telescoping resolution of the identity

The `L¹`-normalized dilates of a fixed profile give an approximate identity,
and their consecutive differences are the Littlewood--Paley pieces: each has
vanishing integral, and the dilates telescope into the low-frequency piece
plus the sum of the differences.  This is the elementary half of BRS (5.7). -/

/-- The `L¹`-normalized dilate `φ_j(x) = 2^j φ(2^j x)`. -/
def brsDilate (φ : ℝ → ℝ) (j : ℕ) (x : ℝ) : ℝ := 2 ^ j * φ (2 ^ j * x)

theorem brsDilate_zero (φ : ℝ → ℝ) (x : ℝ) : brsDilate φ 0 x = φ x := by
  simp [brsDilate]

